    "narrative": "Today\u2019s slate for **Ghost Ride the WHIP** is anchored by elite speed and favorable matchups against high xERA starters. **James Wood** (78.28) is our strongest play, boasting an elite 0.425 xwOBA and a massive +17% boost from a soft matchup against Mike Burrows (4.71 xERA); his presence at the top of the order creates massive upside for Runs. **Corbin Carroll** (73.03) and **Isaac Paredes** (72.13) follow closely, with **Isaac Paredes** benefiting significantly from a generous +14% SP skill adjustment against Miles Mikolas, while **Corbin Carroll** remains an essential start for his elite SB potential despite a slightly tougher draw against Walker Buehler. **Mickey Moniak** (61.81) and **Kyle Karros** (60.80) are surging due to the exploitable 5.28 xERA of Eric Lauer, providing critical depth against a vulnerable arm.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the board was the placement of **Jose Caballero** (40.09). Despite his high ceiling for SB, his score was cratered by an abysmal -13% platoon penalty and a -8% hit from batting 9th against Griffin Jax. He remains in the lineup purely as a specialist for stolen bases, though his efficiency is perilously close to our bench threshold. Conversely, **Dalton Rushing** (42.54) barely avoided the bench; his score was depressed by a -9% platoon disadvantage against a lefty in Kyle Freeland and a suboptimal 8th-spot lineup position. We are monitoring lineup confirmations for **Gabriel Moreno**, **Dalton Rushing**, **Isaac Paredes**, **Alex Freeland**, **Brice Turang**, **Austin Riley**, **James Wood**, **Jose Caballero**, **Mickey Moniak**, **Corbin Carroll**, and **Kyle Karros** closely, as any shift from these projected spots\u2014particularly for hitters like **Brice Turang** and **James Wood**\u2014would necessitate a re-evaluation of our efficiency scores given the premium we place on order-driven production. Our bench remains barren of healthy options today, with **Josh Naylor**, **Tyler Soderstrom**, **Vinnie Pasquantino**, and **Giancarlo Stanton** all unavailable, leaving us thin if any of our active starters are scratched late.",
